# Documentation Prompt Template

Use this prompt when creating, updating, or refining documentation.

## Context

**Project:** [Project Name]
**Documentation Type:** [Guide, API Reference, Tutorial, README, etc.]
**Target Audience:** [Developers, End Users, Contributors, etc.]
**Existing Documentation:** [Links to related docs or previous versions]

### Scope & Purpose

[2-3 sentences describing what this documentation should cover and why it's needed]

### Related Documentation

- [Link to prerequisite docs]
- [Link to complementary docs]
- [Link to reference materials]

---

## Task

**Documentation Goal:**
[What should readers understand or be able to do after reading this?]

**Content to Include:**

1. [Section/topic 1 with brief description]
2. [Section/topic 2 with brief description]
3. [Section/topic 3 with brief description]

**Out of Scope:**

- [What should NOT be covered in this doc]
- [Related topics handled elsewhere]

---

## Content Requirements

### Structure

- Use [Markdown / AsciiDoc / etc.]
- Include table of contents for documents > 500 words
- Use clear headings (H2-H4)
- Include code examples where relevant

### Style & Tone

- Use [UK English / formal / conversational]
- Avoid [jargon without explanation / passive voice / etc.]
- Write for [skill level: beginner / intermediate / advanced]

### Media & Examples

- Include [diagrams/screenshots showing X]
- Provide [code examples in [language]]
- Add [tables/lists for [specific content type]]

### Frontmatter (if applicable)

```yaml
---
title: [Document Title]
description: [One-sentence summary]
file_type: [documentation/instructions/guide]
version: [e.g., 1.0.0]
last_updated: [YYYY-MM-DD]
owners: [e.g., ["@username"]]
tags: [e.g., ["documentation", "guide"]]
status: [active/draft/deprecated]
stability: [stable/experimental/deprecated]
domain: [e.g., automation/governance/tooling]
---
```

---

## Acceptance Criteria

The documentation is complete when:

- [ ] All sections from content checklist are covered
- [ ] Code examples are tested and correct
- [ ] Links to other docs are verified and working
- [ ] Passes linting (Markdown, frontmatter, etc.)
- [ ] Reviewed by [stakeholder/SME]
- [ ] Published to [location]

---

## References

- **Documentation Standards:** [Link to docs standards guide]
- **Style Guide:** [Link to project style guide]
- **Similar Documentation:** [Link to doc with similar structure]
- **API/Feature Reference:** [Link to canonical source material]

---

## Additional Notes

- [Key concepts that must be explained clearly]
- [Common mistakes to avoid]
- [Sections that need extra detail or examples]
